    "narrative": "It is October 13, and as we look at the daily landscape for Ghost Ride the WHIP, the priority remains maximizing stolen base upside while navigating the lean schedule. **Travis Bazzana** serves as our primary offensive engine today, carrying a solid 52.797 score against Freddy Peralta. While a 4.32 xERA for the opposing starter suggests a neutral matchup, **Bazzana** is buoyed by an 8% boost for his presumed #2 spot in the order and a favorable platoon profile that offsets the modest park impact. Given the scarcity of SBs in the current market, **Bazzana**\u2019s ability to generate value on the basepaths makes him a locked-in start despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status.\n\nThe bench remains heavy with high-ceiling assets like **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **James Wood**, and **Josh Naylor**, all of whom are sidelined by team off-days. With **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** also unavailable to fill gaps today, our positional flexibility is restricted. The risk today is minimal regarding weather, but the lack of depth means any late-breaking lineup scratches for **Bazzana** would force us to carry a zero, as there is no late-game pivot available to capture the necessary R and SB production. We are relying entirely on **Bazzana** to provide the core efficiency needed to maintain our Roto standings in a shallow-slate environment.",
